Part 7 — Kernel Modules
Kernel modules are dynamically loadable pieces of kernel code (drivers, filesystems, etc.).

7.1 — Essential Commands

bash
# List all currently loaded modules
lsmod

# Count loaded modules
lsmod | wc -l

# Get info about a specific module
modinfo ext4
modinfo e1000

# See module parameters
modinfo -p ext4

# Search for a module
find /lib/modules/$(uname -r) -name "*.ko*" | grep vfat
7.2 — Load and Unload Modules

bash
# Load a module (with dependency resolution)
sudo modprobe vfat

# Verify it loaded
lsmod | grep vfat

# Unload it
sudo modprobe -r vfat

# Verify it's gone
lsmod | grep vfat
7.3 — Blacklist a Module Permanently

bash
# Create a blacklist file
echo "blacklist nouveau" | sudo tee /etc/modprobe.d/blacklist-nouveau.conf

# Rebuild initramfs so it takes effect at boot
sudo dracut --force

# Reboot and verify
sudo reboot
lsmod | grep nouveau   # Should return nothing
7.4 — Auto-Load a Module at Boot

bash
# Create a modules-load config
echo "vfat" | sudo tee /etc/modules-load.d/vfat.conf

# Reboot and verify
sudo reboot
lsmod | grep vfat   # Should be loaded
